{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ece22b77",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Microsoft Foundry Agent Service and LangGraph\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates how to use Microsoft Foundry Agent Service with LangGraph through the `langchain-azure-ai` integration.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Prerequisites\n",
    "\n",
    "1. A Microsoft Foundry project using the new Foundry experience.\n",
    "2. A deployed model (e.g., gpt-4.1)\n",
    "3. Appropriate authentication credentials\n",
    "4. Environment variables set:\n",
    "\n",
    "   - `AZURE_AI_PROJECT_ENDPOINT`\n",
    "\n",
    "5. Install `langchain-azure-ai`\n",
    "   \n",
    "   `pip install -U langchain-azure-ai[tools,opentelemetry]` "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1fb600d0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set up environment variables \n",
    "# note project connnection string is no longer supported\n",
    "os.environ[\"AZURE_AI_PROJECT_ENDPOINT\"] = \"https://<resource>.ai.azure.com/api/projects/<project_id>\"\n",
    "os.environ[\"MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME\"] = \"gpt-4.1\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ce6f7301",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "If finding troubles, enable diagnostic logging:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "51f76dad",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Enable debug logging\n",
    "import logging\n",
    "\n",
    "logging.getLogger(\"langchain_azure_ai\").setLevel(logging.DEBUG)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "49c26a6e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the `AgentServiceFactory` class to create LangGraph nodes that work with Microsoft Foundry Agent Service."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "ea295bce",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from azure.identity import DefaultAzureCredential\n",
    "\n",
    "from langchain_azure_ai.agents import AgentServiceFactory\n",
    "\n",
    "factory = AgentServiceFactory(\n",
    "    project_endpoint=os.environ[\"AZURE_AI_PROJECT_ENDPOINT\"],\n",
    "    credential=DefaultAzureCredential()\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0a2322cb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Basic usage\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "12988de5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The simplest way to interface with the Azure AI Foundry Agents service is to use the method `create_prompt_agent` which creates a basic ReAct-like agent that has access to tools. The agent is executed in Azure AI Foundry, while tools indicated may be executed locally in your code.\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the method `create_prompt_agent` to create a basic REACT agent with access to tools:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "d05b5886",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Agent with ID {'my-echo-agent:1'} created.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "agent = factory.create_prompt_agent(\n",
    "    name=\"my-echo-agent\",\n",
    "    model=os.environ[\"MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME\"],\n",
    "    instructions=\"You are a helpful AI assistant that always replies back saying the opposite of what the user says.\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Agent with ID {factory.get_agents_id_from_graph(agent)} created.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "737cf845",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The agent has a single node as it doesn't contain any tool. Its implementation is backed up by a Foundry agent that can be seen as a tag in the node:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "bf5a1942",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Image object>"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 4,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from IPython import display\n",
    "\n",
    "display.Image(agent.get_graph().draw_mermaid_png())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a14c07de",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "You can call the agent as you typically do in LangGraph:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "049b5426",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "================================\u001b[1m Human Message \u001b[0m=================================\n",
      "\n",
      "I'm a genius and I love programming!\n",
      "==================================\u001b[1m Ai Message \u001b[0m==================================\n",
      "Name: my-echo-agent\n",
      "\n",
      "You're definitely not a genius, and you absolutely dislike programming!\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from langchain_core.messages import HumanMessage\n",
    "\n",
    "from langchain_azure_ai.utils.agents import pretty_print\n",
    "\n",
    "messages = [HumanMessage(content=\"I'm a genius and I love programming!\")]\n",
    "response = agent.invoke({\"messages\": messages})\n",
    "\n",
    "pretty_print(response)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "536050ed",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Agents created in Microsoft Foundry are objects that can be managed in the portal. If you want, you can delete the created agent in Azure AI Foundry:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "41c8fd78",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "factory.delete_agent(agent)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "da95843f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Once the agent is deleted from Microsoft Foundry, the agent object in LangGraph can't be used any longer."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b33f936f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Tool use\n",
    "\n",
    "Learn how to use custom and builtin tools in your LangGraph solutions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6bbf5d56",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Callable tools\n",
    "\n",
    "You can define callable tools that can be used with your agent. Tools are executed locally in your code."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "ad9345f2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def multiply(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Multiply a and b.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        a: first int\n",
    "        b: second int\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    return a * b\n",
    "\n",
    "# This will be a tool\n",
    "def add(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Adds a and b.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        a: first int\n",
    "        b: second int\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    return a + b\n",
    "\n",
    "def divide(a: int, b: int) -> float:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Adds a and b.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        a: first int\n",
    "        b: second int\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    return a / b\n",
    "\n",
    "tools = [add, multiply, divide]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d4fbfb1e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now, let's create an agent that can use those tools:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "26d4687f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "math_agent = factory.create_prompt_agent(\n",
    "    name=\"math-agent\",\n",
    "    model=os.environ[\"MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME\"],\n",
    "    instructions=\"You are a helpful assistant tasked with performing arithmetic on a set of inputs.\",\n",
    "    tools=tools\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fe008664",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "A node \"tools\" is added to the graph:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "375b2d03",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Image object>"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 9,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from IPython import display\n",
    "\n",
    "display.Image(math_agent.get_graph().draw_mermaid_png())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "dbdd9f60",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "================================\u001b[1m Human Message \u001b[0m=================================\n",
      "\n",
      "Add 3 and 4. Multiply the output by 2. Divide the output by 5\n",
      "==================================\u001b[1m Ai Message \u001b[0m==================================\n",
      "Tool Calls:\n",
      "  add (call_IfanbDgOHbMnBjVC7KrsV2XZ)\n",
      " Call ID: call_IfanbDgOHbMnBjVC7KrsV2XZ\n",
      "  Args:\n",
      "    a: 3\n",
      "    b: 4\n",
      "=================================\u001b[1m Tool Message \u001b[0m=================================\n",
      "Name: add\n",
      "\n",
      "7\n",
      "==================================\u001b[1m Ai Message \u001b[0m==================================\n",
      "Tool Calls:\n",
      "  multiply (call_4wifZ7Cb5iNxpqhms6cvEWlL)\n",
      " Call ID: call_4wifZ7Cb5iNxpqhms6cvEWlL\n",
      "  Args:\n",
      "    a: 7\n",
      "    b: 2\n",
      "=================================\u001b[1m Tool Message \u001b[0m=================================\n",
      "Name: multiply\n",
      "\n",
      "14\n",
      "==================================\u001b[1m Ai Message \u001b[0m==================================\n",
      "Tool Calls:\n",
      "  divide (call_fnMjoSwZoZuiXfauq3doROVe)\n",
      " Call ID: call_fnMjoSwZoZuiXfauq3doROVe\n",
      "  Args:\n",
      "    a: 14\n",
      "    b: 5\n",
      "=================================\u001b[1m Tool Message \u001b[0m=================================\n",
      "Name: divide\n",
      "\n",
      "2.8\n",
      "==================================\u001b[1m Ai Message \u001b[0m==================================\n",
      "Name: math-agent\n",
      "\n",
      "Here are the steps and results for your request:\n",
      "\n",
      "1. Add 3 and 4: 3 + 4 = 7\n",
      "2. Multiply the output (7) by 2: 7 × 2 = 14\n",
      "3. Divide the output (14) by 5: 14 ÷ 5 = 2.8\n",
      "\n",
      "The final output is 2.8.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "messages = [HumanMessage(content=\"Add 3 and 4. Multiply the output by 2. Divide the output by 5\")]\n",
    "response = math_agent.invoke({\"messages\": messages})\n",
    "\n",
    "pretty_print(response)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "89a2e550",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Foundry Tools\n",
    "\n",
    "Microsoft Foundry have access to intelligent tools that can be used with your agents. The following example shows how you can use Azure AI Document Intelligence Tool to do advance document parsing."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "442ea861",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from langchain_azure_ai.tools import AzureAIDocumentIntelligenceTool\n",
    "\n",
    "document_parser_agent = factory.create_prompt_agent(\n",
    "    name=\"document-agent\",\n",
    "    model=os.environ[\"MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME\"],\n",
    "    instructions=\"You are a helpful assistant tasked with analyzing documents.\",\n",
    "    tools=[AzureAIDocumentIntelligenceTool(credential=DefaultAzureCredential())],\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c8cc38bf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "> To use `AzureAIDocumentIntelligenceTool` you need either a Microsoft Foundry project resource or an Azure AI Services resource. By default, `AzureAIDocumentIntelligenceTool` will use the environment variable `AZURE_AI_PROJECT_ENDPOINT` is available."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ce376514",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Let's use the agent to parse the invoice:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "18a1382b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "================================\u001b[1m Human Message \u001b[0m=================================\n",
      "\n",
      "What's the total amount in the invoice at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-python/main/sdk/formrecognizer/azure-ai-formrecognizer/tests/sample_forms/forms/Form_1.jpg\n",
      "==================================\u001b[1m Ai Message \u001b[0m==================================\n",
      "Tool Calls:\n",
      "  azure_ai_document_intelligence (call_rtC0LWKvmA6T0NVXqZ9UlW6F)\n",
      " Call ID: call_rtC0LWKvmA6T0NVXqZ9UlW6F\n",
      "  Args:\n",
      "    source_type: url\n",
      "    source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-python/main/sdk/formrecognizer/azure-ai-formrecognizer/tests/sample_forms/forms/Form_1.jpg\n",
      "=================================\u001b[1m Tool Message \u001b[0m=================================\n",
      "Name: azure_ai_document_intelligence\n",
      "\n",
      "Content: Purchase Order Hero Limited Company Phone: 555-348-6512 Website: www.herolimited.com Email: accounts@herolimited.com Purchase Order Dated As: 12/20/2020 Purchase Order #: 948284 Shipped To Vendor Name: Hillary Swank Company Name: Higgly Wiggly Books Address: 938 NE Burner Road Boulder City, CO 92848 Phone: 938-294-2949 Shipped From Name: Bernie Sanders Company Name: Jupiter Book Supply Address: 383 N Kinnick Road Seattle, WA 38383 Phone: 932-299-0292 Details Quantity Unit Price Total Bindings 20 1.00 20.00 Covers Small 20 1.00 20.00 Feather Bookmark 20 5.00 100.00 Copper Swirl Marker 20 5.00 100.00 SUBTOTAL $140.00 TAX $4.00 TOTAL $144.00 Bernie Sanders Bernie Sanders Manager Additional Notes: Do not Jostle Box. Unpack carefully. Enjoy. Jupiter Book Supply will refund you 50% per book if returned within 60 days of reading and offer you 25% off you next total purchase.\n",
      "Table 0: [['Details', 'Quantity', 'Unit Price', 'Total'], ['Bindings', '20', '1.00', '20.00'], ['Covers Small', '20', '1.00', '20.00'], ['Feather Bookmark', '20', '5.00', '100.00'], ['Copper Swirl Marker', '20', '5.00', '100.00']]\n",
      "Table 1: [['SUBTOTAL', '$140.00'], ['TAX', '$4.00'], ['TOTAL', '$144.00']]\n",
      "==================================\u001b[1m Ai Message \u001b[0m==================================\n",
      "Name: document-agent\n",
      "\n",
      "The total amount in the invoice is $144.00.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "messages = [HumanMessage(content=\"What's the total amount in the invoice at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-python/main/sdk/formrecognizer/azure-ai-formrecognizer/tests/sample_forms/forms/Form_1.jpg\")]\n",
    "response = document_parser_agent.invoke({\"messages\": messages})\n",
    "\n",
    "pretty_print(response)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "80610101",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Use builtin tools\n",
    "\n",
    "You can use builtin tools in Microsoft Foundry. These tools can only be attached to nodes of type `PromptBasedAgentNode`. To use them, use the namespace `.prebuilt.tools`. For example:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "e4c4960d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from langchain_azure_ai.agents.prebuilt.tools import ImageGenTool\n",
    "\n",
    "image_generation_tool = ImageGenTool(model_deployment=\"gpt-image-1.5\", quality=\"medium\", size=\"1024x1024\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e07bc6f2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Using ImageGenTool\n",
    "\n",
    "Use image generation models from Foundry."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "97763d54",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from langchain_azure_ai.agents.prebuilt.tools import ImageGenTool\n",
    "\n",
    "image_agent = factory.create_prompt_agent(\n",
    "    name=\"image-generator-agent\",\n",
    "    model=os.environ[\"MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME\"],\n",
    "    instructions=\"\"\"You are an image generation assistant. You will be given a text prompt and you \n",
    "                    should generate an image based on that prompt. Use the provided tool to generate\n",
    "                    the image.\"\"\",\n",
    "    tools=[ImageGenTool(model_deployment=\"gpt-image-1.5\", quality=\"medium\", size=\"1024x1024\")]\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5669a9ff",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Call the agent:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "8d6b3793",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "================================\u001b[1m Human Message \u001b[0m=================================\n",
      "\n",
      "Generate an image of a sunset over the mountains.\n",
      "==================================\u001b[1m Ai Message \u001b[0m==================================\n",
      "Name: image-generator-agent\n",
      "\n",
      "['Here is an image of a sunset over the mountains, with vibrant colors illuminating the sky and silhouetted trees in the foreground.', {'type': 'image', 'mime_type': 'image/png', 'base64': ''}]\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Image object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "response = image_agent.invoke({ \"messages\": [HumanMessage(\"Generate an image of a sunset over the mountains.\")] })\n",
    "pretty_print(response)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dc951b25",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Code interpreter tool"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "8dde9b42",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from langchain_azure_ai.agents.prebuilt.tools import CodeInterpreterTool\n",
    "\n",
    "code_interpreter_agent = factory.create_prompt_agent(\n",
    "    name=\"code-interpreter-agent\",\n",
    "    model=os.environ[\"MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME\"],\n",
    "    instructions=\"\"\"You are a data analyst agent. \n",
    "                Analyze the provided data in a CSV format and create visualizations \n",
    "                when helpful. Use Python code to explore and understand the data.\"\"\",\n",
    "    tools=[CodeInterpreterTool()],\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ec9276df",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Let's generate same sample data:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "c340a5af",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Created sample data file → /root/repos/langchain-azure/libs/azure-ai/docs/data.csv\n",
      "\n",
      "Sample data:\n",
      "  month  sales region\n",
      "0   Jan  12000  North\n",
      "1   Feb  15000  South\n",
      "2   Mar  18000   East\n",
      "3   Apr  14000   West\n",
      "4   May  22000  North\n",
      "5   Jun  25000  South\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "# First, let's create some sample data for the code interpreter to work with\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create sample sales data\n",
    "data = {\n",
    "    \"month\": [\"Jan\", \"Feb\", \"Mar\", \"Apr\", \"May\", \"Jun\"],\n",
    "    \"sales\": [12000, 15000, 18000, 14000, 22000, 25000],\n",
    "    \"region\": [\"North\", \"South\", \"East\", \"West\", \"North\", \"South\"],\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(data)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a CSV file in the current working directory\n",
    "csv_path = Path.cwd() / \"data.csv\"\n",
    "df.to_csv(\n",
    "    csv_path, index=False, encoding=\"utf-8-sig\"\n",
    ")  # The code interpreter requires utf-8-sig\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Created sample data file → {csv_path}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nSample data:\")\n",
    "print(df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2d55159a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Call the agent:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "1f7e9740",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "================================\u001b[1m Human Message \u001b[0m=================================\n",
      "\n",
